\section*{Ethics Statement}

This work uses publicly available programming problems from HumanEval \citep{chen2021evaluating} and MBPP-sanitized \citep{austin2021program}.
All execution traces and pass/fail labels are generated through fully automated program execution; no human annotators or participants were involved.
The dataset contains only source code and execution outputs with no personally identifiable information, offensive content, or privacy-sensitive data.
All experiments were conducted on a single RTX PRO 6000 GPU, representing modest computational costs and environmental impact.
We will publicly release our code, dataset, and trained LoRA adapters to support reproducibility and future research.

